	"notes": "H-9, the scripted runs: a fixed 16-turn transcript sent to each pinned model three times under each of the three eviction policies, with the product's own planTurn deciding what is sent for a context of 8,192 tokens (PREREGISTRATION.md, Amendments 2 and 3). It is not a launcher campaign: eviction-script.mts talks to the runtime's native API, which is where the prompt-evaluation counts are. probe.jsonl is the probe made before it: the runtime reports the whole prompt as evaluated whether it was cached or not, so re-processed tokens are estimated from prompt-evaluation time, the fallback Amendment 3 recorded in advance. The machine and its load in this file are those of the agentic campaign's manifest, written 9 minutes before these runs started; the runs took 1,731 seconds. No estimate of that time was made from the datasheets; my estimate before they started was about 40 minutes."
